From ffd03f1dec5ed30c78ca3104ff799f3ca72011a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:44:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tests): host-wide cap on concurrent per-file pytest
 processes across runs [daveey]

Every run_tests_parallel run sized its pool to os.cpu_count() without knowing about other runs. With
four agent worktrees testing at once, 39 of 67 runnable processes on a 16-core Mac were pytest, the load
average passed 250, and the gateway's Discord heartbeat kept failing. Each per-file attempt now runs
while holding one of HERMES_TEST_HOST_SLOTS (default cpu_count) flock slots in HERMES_TEST_SLOT_DIR
(default /tmp/hermes-test-slots-<uid>), shared by every run on the host. A crashed run frees its slots
with its fds. Children get HERMES_TEST_SLOT_HELD=1 so a run nested in a test never waits on its
parent's slot; HERMES_TEST_HOST_SLOTS=0 disables the cap. run_tests.sh forwards the three variables.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
